.TH SYS_PROC_FDS 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_fds \- list file descriptors for a process
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_fds(pid_t " pid ", sys_fd_t *" fds ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_fds ()
attempts to enumerate open file descriptors for process
.IR pid .
The output array is
.I fds
with element count supplied and returned through
.IR *count .
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negative value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSYS
Current kernel implementation is a stub.
.SH NOTES
Wired in native dispatch, currently unimplemented in kernel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR sys_proc_list (2),
.BR open (2)
